1
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:04,940
Hello everyone and welcome back to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:05,560
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:10,020
And my name is Catherine and today we have a cold lesson.

4
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:10,860
That's right.

5
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:18,180
It's the winter season and of course it gets cold in a lot of different places around the world and so we're going to talk about heating.

6
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:25,480
Okay, this is very important but before we do get started, we have a very important word to preview in Vocabulary Preview.

7
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:27,490
Vocabulary Preview.

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:34,080
Alright, so we're going to preview the word freezing.

9
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,750
It is freezing today by the way so this is very appropriate.

10
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:39,750
Freezing means very, very, very cold.

11
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:41,490
Okay, it is freezing.

12
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:43,210
Okay, so it's very cold.

13
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:44,410
It's freezing today.

14
00:00:44,910 --> 00:00:49,890
It's so cold in fact you can't have water outside because the water will become ice.

15
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:50,690
It will freeze.

16
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,040
Okay, great word.

17
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:55,670
So let's listen to our dialogue for the very first time.

18
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,480
It's freezing in here.

19
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:04,500
Can I turn up the heat?

20
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:06,500
Don't touch that thermostat.

21
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:08,460
You don't pay the bills around here.

22
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:09,980
Dad, are you serious?

23
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:12,720
What's the point of having central heating if we can't use it?

24
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:15,730
Look, I can see my breath.

25
00:01:16,270 --> 00:01:17,230
Put on a sweater.

26
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:21,250
I'm not going to let you run up my heating bill just because it's a bit chilly.

27
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:24,160
Dad, I'm going to catch a cold.

28
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:28,150
When I was your age, my parents didn't have central heating like you do.

29
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:31,310
We had a furnace in the center of the living room and that was it.

30
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:34,750
We used it to cook, heat the house, and even dry our clothes.

31
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,390
We never caught a cold.

32
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:37,810
You should be grateful.

33
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:46,450
Alright, we're back and this is actually what a lot of dads are like I think around the world.

34
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:50,840
Yep, my dad definitely liked to keep the heat low in the house.

35
00:01:50,930 --> 00:01:57,750
Alright, so we'll talk about that a little bit later but let's take a look at some four words on Language Takeaway today.

36
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:00,800
Language Takeaway

37
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:06,030
Well, this first word is important for anyone who has a home with heating.

38
00:02:06,790 --> 00:02:08,010
It's called a thermostat.

39
00:02:08,210 --> 00:02:09,710
Alright, a thermostat.

40
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:11,490
What is a thermostat?

41
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:21,670
A thermostat is a dial or like a device on the wall that tells you how hot or how cold the house is.

42
00:02:21,830 --> 00:02:23,550
It's like a thermometer for your house.

43
00:02:23,830 --> 00:02:28,970
Okay, so you can move the thermostat, the temperature to make the house warmer or colder, right?

44
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:36,560
Right, so if it says it's 20 degrees and I think that's too cold, I can turn the thermostat up to 23 degrees.

45
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:45,020
Alright, and well very much related to a thermostat and what this device does is our next word, central heating.

46
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,980
Right, so if you have central heating, you have a thermostat.

47
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:58,880
It's the way to control the heat and central heating means that you have one heater for the whole house and so the air comes into all the different rooms.

48
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:05,610
So not many places in China have this but for example in the United States, in Canada, it is very common.

49
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:13,760
Okay, so your house or your apartment building will have central heating and then you can control how cold or warm the house is with thermostats.

50
00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:14,130
Exactly.

51
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:20,080
Very good and well our next word is related to temperature and it's chilly.

52
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:26,200
Chilly, okay, so there's a big difference between chilly and freezing.

53
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:27,450
Freezing means very very very cold.

54
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,000
Chilly means a little cold.

55
00:03:30,010 --> 00:03:31,550
Right, so it's a little cold.

56
00:03:31,730 --> 00:03:32,310
It's a bit chilly.

57
00:03:33,010 --> 00:03:35,410
Right, so it's a bit chilly today, I'm going to wear a hat.

58
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:41,570
Okay, if it's freezing, I'm going to wear a hat and mittens and a scarf and coat and boots.

59
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:52,160
Right, so if it's a bit chilly, it's not very cold and well moving on, the dad mentioned about him having a furnace when he was young.

60
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:57,550
That's right, the dad had a furnace in his house and the furnace is a way to heat your house.

61
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:58,830
It's like a stove.

62
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:02,370
So yeah, just consider it like a big oven, right?

63
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:08,960
Maybe you've seen it in the old movies where you would have to throw firewood into the furnace to make it heat up the house.

64
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:14,350
Exactly, and so this is very common in older homes and not very common in apartments.

65
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:20,150
Right, and well, that's all the words we have for language takeaway today.

